From c5cb1548967406453c52681889c369aa6a8365e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nicktoper <ntoper@manycore.io>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 13:03:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] self-qa: correct the sweep skill's surfaces and harden
 worklist parsing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The skill named two report surfaces keyed on "when run under a task". The
code has three, keyed on whether the task is *recurring*: a recurring period
task writes slug-keyed entries to the template's durable `retires.md`, any
other task appends the report section to its own blackboard, and a run with
no task writes to stdout. It also hardcoded `autoclose-merged` where
`durable_retire_list` derives the template from the slug. Reconciled in both
tracked copies, and rewrapped an over-long line in the recurring template.

`parse_retire_list` guarded on `RETIRE_LIST_HEADING in text` but partitioned
on the heading *plus its newline*, so a worklist ending exactly at the heading
put the whole file in `header` and re-appended the heading below it — silently
doubling it. A stripped trailing newline is a benign thing for an editor to
do, so normalize it rather than failing the daily sweep over it.

`blackboard_from_env` stays hoisted above the branch that writes the report:
